.TH PLAYLIST-CHECKER 1 "October 2026" "playlist-checker 1.3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
playlist-checker \- check IPTV and internet radio playlists for dead streams and duplicates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B playlist-checker
.RI [ PLAYLIST | URL | LIST.txt ]...
.br
.B playlist-checker
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B playlist-checker
is a desktop application that opens TV (IPTV) and internet radio playlists in
M3U, M3U8, PLS and XSPF format, from files, whole folders (including
subfolders) or web addresses, and checks every stream.
.PP
It recognises HTTP and HTTPS streams, HLS (it tests the real video segment),
Icecast and Shoutcast radio, and RTMP, RTSP and MMS servers. Per-channel
User-Agent and Referer settings (#EXTVLCOPT, or url|User-Agent=...) are used
when checking.
.PP
Duplicates (same stream address, optionally same channel name) are marked.
Groups can be included, excluded, renamed, merged and reordered. A new clean
playlist can be saved, keeping channel logos, EPG information (tvg-id,
url-tvg) and player options, optionally as one file per group. A CSV report of
the check can be exported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PLAYLIST
Playlist files to open at start.
.TP
.I URL
Web addresses (http:// or https://) of playlists to download at start.
.TP
.I LIST.txt
A text file with one playlist address per line. Every playlist is downloaded
(four at a time) and its channels are added; see LISTS OF PLAYLIST ADDRESSES.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH LISTS OF PLAYLIST ADDRESSES
File \(-> Open list of playlist URLs (Ctrl+L) reads a .txt file with one
address per line. Empty lines and lines starting with #, ; or // are ignored,
and text before an address is allowed. Addresses that return a single stream
are added as one channel, local playlist files are opened, and addresses that
fail are listed at the end. Stop cancels the remaining downloads. With
Settings \(-> Check new channels automatically after loading, the new channels
are checked as soon as they are loaded. An example list is installed in
.IR /usr/share/doc/playlist-checker/examples/ .
.SH PLAYLIST COLORS
Every playlist gets its own color: a colored square at the start of each
channel row and, unless switched off in Settings \(-> Tint rows with the
playlist color, a light tint of the row. The Playlists list on the left shows
the colors with the number of channels; click a playlist to show only its
channels, or its \(OK box to leave it out. Unticked groups and playlists are
hidden from the channel list (Settings \(-> Hide unticked groups and playlists
in the channel list), skipped by Check streams and Recheck offline, and left
out of the saved playlist.
.SH USER-AGENT
Some IPTV providers only answer certain players. Settings \(-> User-Agent lets
the program identify itself as VLC, FFmpeg, mpv, Kodi, ExoPlayer, TiviMate,
IPTV Smarters, a Samsung or LG smart TV, an Enigma2 receiver, a web browser
and others, or as any custom text. A User-Agent set inside the playlist for a
channel (#EXTVLCOPT:http-user-agent or url|User-Agent=...) always wins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/playlist-checker/settings.json
User settings (check timeout, User-Agent, duplicate rules, Settings menu options).
.SH NOTES
UDP and multicast links can only be tested inside the provider's own network
and are reported as "not checked".
.PP
Channels are played with VLC or mpv when one of them is installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/antoxa78/PyPlaylist-Checker
